[p175]       8.1.     FLOW-001 Bounded Workflow Configuration
[p175] 
[p175] 
[p175] Authorised administrators must be able to configure supported pricing-specific workflow
[p175] behaviour through a bounded Workflow Configuration Profile.
[p175] 
[p175] A Workflow Configuration Profile may define supported parameters including:
[p175] 
[p175]    ● whether formal review requirements apply within the canonical In Review stage;
[p175]    ● required reviewer roles or participants;
[p175]    ● applicable organisational decision path;
[p175]    ● item-level approval requirements where applicable;
[p175]    ● required approver roles;
[p175]    ● supported sequential or multiple-approval arrangements;
[p175]    ● supported approval-routing conditions;
[p175]    ● target response dates or approval deadlines;
[p175]    ● supported escalation behaviour;
[p175]    ● authorised delegates where organisational policy permits.
[p175] 
[p175] Where policy authorisation is enabled, the Workflow Configuration Profile may determine
[p175] whether eligible pricing work is routed into the policy-authorisation path rather than item-level
[p175] approval.
[p175] 
[p176] Workflow configuration must not independently define policy-authorisation eligibility,
[p176] authority, qualification thresholds or policy conditions.
[p176] 
[p176] Those requirements remain governed by FLOW-022, FLOW-023, GOV-027 and GOV-028.
[p176] 
[p176] Workflow Configuration Profiles must operate within the canonical Pricing Initiative lifecycle
[p176] defined in Section 2.2.
[p176] 
[p176] Administrators must not be able to use workflow configuration to:
[p176] 
[p176]     ● create new Pricing Initiative lifecycle states;
[p176]     ● redefine the meaning of canonical lifecycle states;
[p176]     ● create arbitrary state-transition graphs;
[p176]     ● redefine Pricing Proposal status or validity;
[p176]     ● create unrestricted custom workflow stages;
[p176]     ● execute user-authored scripts or code;
[p176]     ● introduce arbitrary executable expressions;
[p176]     ● create arbitrary user-defined triggers or action chains;
[p176]     ● perform general-purpose organisational automation;
[p176]     ● bypass Proposal readiness requirements;
[p176]     ● bypass approval authority;
[p176]     ● bypass maker-checker requirements;
[p176]     ● bypass Guardrails or other Governance controls.
[p176] 
[p176] Routing and escalation conditions must use supported pricing-specific condition types
[p176] exposed by the MVP.
[p176] 
[p176] A Workflow Configuration Profile therefore configures supported behaviour inside the
[p176] Owómidé pricing lifecycle rather than defining a new workflow engine.
[p176] 
[p176]

[p193]      8.31.      FLOW-031 Workflow Visibility
[p193] 
[p193] 
[p193] Relevant users must be able to understand:
[p193] 
[p193]     ● current workflow state;
[p193]     ● completed stages;
[p193]     ● outstanding stages;
[p193]     ● current responsible party;
[p193]     ● required next action;
[p193]     ● pending approvals;
[p193]     ● blocking issues.
