[p200] 
[p200] An analyst must not automatically receive formal approval authority.
[p200] 
[p200]

[p202]     9.13.     GOV-013 Auditor
[p202] 
[p202] 
[p202] An Auditor may inspect relevant historical pricing records, including where authorised:
[p202] 
[p202]    ● proposals;
[p202]    ● versions;
[p202]    ● approvals;
[p202]    ● policy-authorisation records;
[p202]    ● workflow history;
[p202]    ● execution history;
[p202]    ● administrative changes;
[p202]    ● audit records.
[p202] 
[p202] Audit access is read-only unless additional permissions are explicitly granted.
[p202] 
[p202]

[p202]     9.15.     GOV-015 Permission Categories
[p202] 
[p203] The permission system must distinguish actions such as:
[p203] 
[p203]    ● View;
[p203]    ● Create;
[p203]    ● Edit;
[p203]    ● Analyse;
[p203]    ● Comment;
[p203]    ● Assign;
[p203]    ● Review;
[p203]    ● Submit;
[p203]    ● Approve;
[p203]    ● Reject;
[p203]    ● Request Changes;
[p203]    ● Execute;
[p203]    ● Configure;
[p203]    ● Export;
[p203]    ● Audit.
[p203] 
[p203] Permissions must be evaluated against the relevant resource and scope.
[p203] 
[p203]

[p203]     9.16.      GOV-016 Resource-Level Permissions
[p203] 
[p203] 
[p203] Permissions must apply to defined resource types such as:
[p203] 
[p203]    ● organisation settings;
[p203]    ● users;
[p203]    ● pricing data;
[p203]    ● costs;
[p203]    ● Pricing Initiatives;
[p203]    ● Pricing Builder logic;
[p203]    ● scenarios;
[p203]    ● Pricing Proposals;
[p203]    ● approvals;
[p203]    ● policy-authorisation records;
[p203]    ● execution records;
[p203]    ● monitoring information;
[p203]    ● audit history.
[p203] 
[p204] A user may therefore have different authority across different product objects.
[p204] 
[p204]

[p204]      9.17.      GOV-017 Scope-Based Authority
[p204] 
[p204] 
[p204] Permissions must support limiting authority by organisational scope.
[p204] 
[p204] Relevant scopes may include:
[p204] 
[p204]     ● business unit;
[p204]     ● category;
[p204]     ● product group;
[p204]     ● product;
[p204]     ● region;
[p204]     ● location;
[p204]     ● channel;
[p204]     ● customer group;
[p204]     ● vendor;
[p204]     ● price list.
[p204] 
[p204] A user authorised for one scope must not automatically gain authority outside that scope.
[p204] 
[p204]

[p205]      9.21.       GOV-021 Cost Visibility
[p205] 
[p205] 
[p205] Access to sensitive cost information must be independently controllable.
[p205] 
[p205] A user may participate in pricing work without necessarily being permitted to view cost data.
[p205] 
[p205] Cost visibility controls must apply across:
[p205] 
[p205]     ● product records;
[p205]     ● initiative context;
[p205]     ● analysis;
[p205]     ● scenarios;
[p205]     ● proposals;
[p205]     ● exports;
[p205]     ● AI interactions.
[p205]

[p209]      9.26.      GOV-026 Approval Authority Levels
[p209] 
[p210] Where required, the organisation must be able to define approval authority according to
[p210] supported thresholds.
[p210] 
[p210] Authority may depend on factors such as:
[p210] 
[p210]    ● magnitude of price change;
[p210]    ● margin level;
[p210]    ● discount level;
[p210]    ● category;
[p210]    ● business unit;
[p210]    ● commercial significance;
[p210]    ● geographic or channel scope.
[p210] 
[p210] A user must not approve work exceeding their configured authority.
[p210] 
[p210]

[p212]      9.30.    GOV-030 AI Permission Inheritance
[p212] 
[p212] 
[p212] AI must operate using the permission context of the user invoking it.
[p212] 
[p213] AI must not access or reveal:
[p213] 
[p213]    ● resources outside the user's scope;
[p213]    ● restricted cost information;
[p213]    ● pricing initiatives the user cannot access;
[p213]    ● protected historical records;
[p213]    ● unavailable organisational information.
[p213]

[p213]     9.33.       GOV-033 User Suspension and Revocation
[p213] 
[p213] 
[p213] Suspending or deactivating a user must immediately prevent new protected actions.
[p213] 
[p213] Existing:
[p213] 
[p214]    ● comments;
[p214]    ● analyses;
[p214]    ● submissions;
[p214]    ● approvals;
[p214]    ● policy-authorisation records;
[p214]    ● execution records;
[p214]    ● audit events
[p214] 
[p214] must remain preserved.
[p214] 
[p214]

[p215]      9.36.      GOV-036 Governance Audit Trail
[p215] 
[p215] 
[p215] Consequential governance actions must be recorded with:
[p215] 
[p215]    ● actor;
[p215]    ● action;
[p215] 
[p216]    ● affected user or configuration;
[p216]    ● timestamp;
[p216]    ● previous state where relevant;
